# Services set to Start=4 (Disabled) OFFLINE on the Windows CI golden by
# apply-offline-service-payloads.sh (payload `ci-background-off`), one per line.
# Every VM cloned from that golden runs ONE job and is then destroyed, so
# background maintenance can only compete with the job for its 4 vCPUs. On
# 2026-09-30, TiWorker, wuaucltcore and SearchIndexer together had used about
# 75 CPU-minutes of a job VM within 2 h. Rationale: ../windows-x64-base/ci-toolchain-golden.md.
#
# Windows Update: the service, the orchestrator that schedules scans and
# installs (the UpdateOrchestrator scheduled tasks all go through it), the
# Medic service that re-enables both, and Delivery Optimization (update
# download peer-to-peer). UsoSvc and WaaSMedicSvc refuse an ONLINE change even
# from an elevated administrator, which is why this is an offline edit.
# Start=4 alone does NOT hold for these three: on 2026-10-23, on clones of a
# golden whose servicing was ~3 weeks old, SYSTEM switched WaaSMedicSvc to
# demand start during boot (System event 7040 logged by services.exe a few
# seconds after the SCM came up, no scheduled task involved), and wuauserv /
# UsoSvc ~1 min later. The same golden had stayed off when it was fresh. So
# ci-background-off-system.reg also replaces their SCM security descriptor
# (Services\<svc>\Security\Security) with one that denies Everyone, SYSTEM
# included, change-config / write-DAC / write-owner / delete:
#   O:SYG:SYD:(D;;DCSDWDWO;;;WD)(A;;RC;;;OW)(A;;CCLCSWRPWPDTLOCRRC;;;SY)
#     (A;;CCLCSWRPWPDTLOCRRC;;;BA)(A;;CCLCSWRPLORC;;;AU)
#     S:(AU;FA;CCDCLCSWRPWPDTLOSDRCWDWO;;;WD)
# The OWNER RIGHTS entry removes the owner's implicit WRITE_DAC. The SACL, the
# AU entry and the SY owner/group are the stock descriptor's (an SD without an
# owner and group makes the SCM fail OpenService with 1338, which was tried).
# The SCM reads it at boot and checks every ChangeServiceConfig against it.
wuauserv
UsoSvc
WaaSMedicSvc
DoSvc
# Windows Search (SearchIndexer.exe).
WSearch
# Microsoft Store Install Service. Its scheduled task
# \Microsoft\Windows\InstallService\ScanForUpdates is a COM handler that runs
# in taskhostw, so disabling the Windows Update services does not stop it, and
# it switches wuauserv back to demand start and starts it (measured
# 2026-09-30 on a clone: ~6 min after boot, then a scan every ~15 s and
# TiWorker). With InstallService disabled the task still runs but leaves
# wuauserv Disabled. The gate triggers it (ci-background-off.trigger-tasks).
InstallService
